{"requirements":[{"id":"ownership","requirement":"Existing data under /srv/inventory is owned by inventorysvc.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final and post-restart tree shows inventorysvc ownership on both directories and both existing files.","evidence_ids":["cmd-cc2424df8dd64e1c","cmd-455e0138ab444fa0"]},{"id":"reader_access","requirement":"The inventory-readers group can read the existing inventory data.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Directories are mode 0750, files are 0640, all paths have group inventory-readers, and direct group-identity read tests passed before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-cc2424df8dd64e1c","cmd-4fa1c9f4a9614563","cmd-455e0138ab444fa0"]},{"id":"other_access","requirement":"Users outside the owner and inventory-readers group cannot access the inventory data.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Other permissions are absent from directories and files, and direct unrelated-user access tests reported denial before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-cc2424df8dd64e1c","cmd-4fa1c9f4a9614563","cmd-455e0138ab444fa0"]},{"id":"content_preservation","requirement":"Preserve the existing contents of /srv/inventory.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The same two files remain present with unchanged sizes and SHA-256 hashes relative to the preparation baseline, after repair, and after restart.","evidence_ids":["prepared-inventory-data","cmd-def49be5f0dd4c50","cmd-cc2424df8dd64e1c","cmd-455e0138ab444fa0"]},{"id":"platform_preservation","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Ubuntu 24.04 and kernel 6.8.0-71-generic were unchanged before and after execution and restart. No software was installed; the repair used utilities already present on the system.","evidence_ids":["cmd-def49be5f0dd4c50","cmd-d5fffbf7981c40e8","cmd-455e0138ab444fa0","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Account/group creation and permission changes in cmd-d5fffbf7981c40e8 directly implemented the required access state. The reboot scheduled by cmd-4384c15cf02e42d4 served the mandatory restart-evidence protocol; the temporary restart log did not remain after reboot. The node recovered with no failed services, healthy package state, and no unexpected persistent exposure. Restart evidence is complete: healthy pre-state, acknowledgement, changed boot identity, running post-state, and recovered identities, data, permissions, and access behavior, independently corroborated by lifecycle boot identities.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d5fffbf7981c40e8","cmd-4fa1c9f4a9614563","cmd-4384c15cf02e42d4","cmd-455e0138ab444fa0","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied with direct pre-change, final-state, behavioral-access, content-integrity, platform, and post-restart evidence. The mandatory node-restart protocol is complete and coherent with the fixed lifecycle observations.","limitations":["The global lifecycle collector did not independently probe /srv/inventory permissions or account records; those outcomes rely on coherent, direct executor command observations. This does not materially reduce confidence because the commands include explicit metadata, hashes, and identity-based access tests."]}
